##Comprehensive Summary: go.py Orchestrator1. Functional RolesThe script operates as a "State Machine" with three distinct modes of existence, determined by terminal flags:Discovery Mode (--ticker): Queries the model for a specific stock’s "physics" profile (Confidence + Rank).Research Mode (--top): Generates the uncorrelated Top 10 list for manual observation.Execution Mode (--live): Connects the full pipeline—Audit, Risk, Compliance, and Execution.2. The Execution Pipeline (The 5-Step Loop)When running in its most complete state, go.py follows this sequence to ensure zero-error logic:Inference (The Brain): Calls variables/00_meta_learner.py to get the raw probability scores for the S&P 500 based on your V01–V08 state variables.Filter (The Diversity Gate): Feeds those scores into correlation_logic.py. This step prunes the list to the Top 10 most confident stocks that have low mathematical correlation.Audit & Risk (The CFO): Calls risk_manager.py. It pings the broker for your live balance ($10,321), subtracts your 20% cash reserve, and calculates exactly how many dollars each of the 10 tickers deserves.Compliance (The Lawyer): Consults firm_rules.py. If the proposed trades violate a Daily Loss Limit or a news-trading window, it "trims" the order size before it ever leaves your computer.Transmission (The Hands): Sends the final, vetted Mid-point Limit Orders to broker_connection.py.Visualizing the FlowInternal Architecture (The "Clean" Setup)BlockSource Filego.py InteractionData Ingestiondata/ticker_cache/Reads local OHLCV to save on API credits/latency.Logic Filtercorrelation_logic.pyImported internally to filter the 500-stock matrix into 10.Compliancefirm_rules.pyActs as a "Safety Wrapper" around the risk_manager output.Executionbroker_connection.pyThe final destination for the order payload.The "One-Command" LifestyleBecause of this setup, you can check your model's status from your laptop during a lecture at Berkeley with a single line:python go.py --topThis provides a No-Stakes Validation of your math. You can see the Top 10, check the prices, and verify if the model's "physics" are playing out in real-time before you ever flip the switch to LIVE.Final VerdictThis architecture is the "Golden Ratio" for your current stage. It’s lightweight enough for a Proof of Concept, but structured enough to scale into Phase 2 (Tech Launch) without needing a total rewrite. You are building a system that is easy to debug, impossible to accidentally "blow up," and mathematically aligned with your 2026 graduation goals.